From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8350: keep the PCIe GDSCs in retention

The Qualcomm PCIe controller keeps the link up across system suspend
when an endpoint is present (the QCA6390 Wi-Fi on PCIe0 on the Galaxy
Z Flip3). With PWRSTS_OFF_ON, genpd switches pcie_0_gdsc off in the
noirq phase of suspend-to-idle and the SoC cold-resets there: pm_test
"devices" survives, "platform" resets.

Let the PCIe GDSCs only go to retention, as SM8450, SM8550 and SC8280XP
already do. The same fix was found on the REDMAGIC 6 (SteamOS-ARM-
Handhelds, kernel-sm8350 patch 0014). s2idle now suspends and resumes,
woken by the RTC alarm and by the fold sensor.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c
@@ -3421,7 +3421,7 @@ static struct gdsc pcie_0_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc pcie_1_gdsc = {
@@ -3429,7 +3429,7 @@ static struct gdsc pcie_1_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_1_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc ufs_card_gdsc = {
